 [:db/cas [:question/id #uuid "c8fd3ad8-a86b-542f-ab4a-6226468a4f6c"] :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F=⟨0,\\,-z,\\,2y⟩$ and the closed surface $S$ that encloses the finite region between the cone $z=4-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ and the plane $z=0.$ Let $D$ be the projection of $S$ onto the $xy$-plane. The flux of $F$ across $S$ can be expressed in terms of a double integral as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∬}_{D}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be the missing expression?" "Consider the vector field $F=⟨0,\\,-z,\\,2y⟩$ and the closed surface $S$ that encloses the finite region between the cone $z=4-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ and the plane $z=0.$ Let $D$ be the projection of $S$ onto the $xy$-plane. The flux of $F$ across $S$ can be expressed in terms of a double integral as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∬}_{D}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWhich expression belongs in the blank when the upper and lower surfaces are parametrized as graphs over $D$ and their outward flux integrands are added pointwise where defined, before integration?"]
